  "text": "Scattered across it stand smooth bone-colored forms, part machine part, part larva, each casting a hard directional shadow though no sun, and a woman climbs in beside its driver, leaving her labor and her leisure behind without protest. Some cling on. A computer is a brain with memory, attention and fatigue. A woman's body keeps dissolving into rivers, into other women's bodies, as though the object generates its own tail like a snake calendar. Nobody rides it. A nightingale sings itself to death for love of a rose that will outlast it by many seasons, trading beauty for complaint across a garden wall.",
